---
// Part 1 — copy from "Copy update 28 Sept" (docs/), one 70ch column. Each of
// the doc's section breaks opens on a full-bleed <Scene>; the photographs are
// from Unsplash (credits in src/assets/story/README.md).
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Scene from '../components/Scene.astro';
import ReadProgress from '../components/ReadProgress.astro';
import crowd from '../assets/story/problem-01-crowd-police.jpg';
import greenwich from '../assets/story/problem-02-greenwich-flag.jpg';
import march from '../assets/story/problem-03-march.jpg';
import armsLinked from '../assets/story/problem-04-arms-linked.jpg';
---

<Layout title="Our Real Problem — We The People" introLines={['Our Real', 'Problem']}>
  <PageHero lines={['Our Real', 'Problem']}>
    <p class="hero__kicker fade-up">Part 01</p>
  </PageHero>

  <ReadProgress />
  <article class="prose">
    <Scene
      first
      eager
      src={crowd}
      alt="A packed crowd on a British street at dusk, police officers in hi-vis among them"
      heading="We all know things are going wrong. We all feel it."
    />

    <p class="lead">
      Like you, everyone has their own list: cost of living, inequality, immigration, the
      march to war, the climate, the water, the trains, even potholes…
    </p>
    <p>Whatever we care about, effective action is so rarely taken.</p>
    <p>
      And we're left feeling disillusioned, angry, afraid and powerless above all.
    </p>

    <Scene
      src={greenwich}
      alt="A Union Jack hanging from the stone colonnades of the Old Royal Naval College, Greenwich"
      heading="The old way of entrusting politicians isn't working"
    />
    <p>
      It's not clear if any politicians put our interests first – or even if they could,
      given the swamp of bureaucracy, finance and pressures of the global system with which
      they contend.
    </p>
    <p>
      The promise of elections tells us that if things are going wrong, we can elect
      someone different, someone better. Yet how often have we voted with high hopes, only
      to be let down?
    </p>
    <p>No wonder trust in politicians is the lowest it's ever been.</p>
    <p>And more and more people are losing faith in the system itself.</p>

    <Scene
      src={march}
      alt="A vast crowd of marchers with placards filling a city street, police watching from a bridge above"
      heading="Our real danger"
    />
    <p>Plenty of people think this is just an efficiency problem.</p>
    <p>
      If politicians delivered, and things worked better, then everything would go back to
      normal.
    </p>
    <p>But something deeper and far more dangerous stands in the way.</p>

    <h2>We are becoming tribal</h2>
    <p>
      A perfect storm of social alienation, economic pressure, social and partisan media, is
      driving us deeply apart.
    </p>
    <p>
      Politicians don't help. Most pitch to one tribe or other in their quest for power.
    </p>
    <p>Our current system of democracy is not designed for this.</p>
    <p>Our elections rely on the losers accepting defeat.</p>
    <p>
      But in a tribal society, it is highly unlikely that one side will consent to the rule
      of the other.
    </p>
    <p>
      This kind of division has ushered in dictatorships or even led to civil war in other
      places, at other times.
    </p>

    <Scene
      src={armsLinked}
      alt="Two young men at a march, arms round each other, fists raised to a blue sky"
      focus="50% 30%"
      heading="But We The People still believe in democracy"
    />
    <p>
      We believe we can rediscover our ability to talk, listen and compromise no matter how
      difficult it seems right now.
    </p>
    <p>It will not happen through politicians, political parties or elections.</p>
    <p>We need something new.</p>

    <p class="pull">That is what this project is all about.</p>

    <a class="back" href="/hope">Our Real Hope →</a>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    var back = document.querySelector('article.prose .back');
    if (!back) return;
    var fired = false;
    var observer = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      entries.forEach(function (entry) {
        if (entry.isIntersecting && !fired) {
          fired = true;
          window.posthog?.capture('problem_article_read');
          observer.disconnect();
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.5 });
    observer.observe(back);
  });
</script>
